%% RIFT — MCP integration flow (actual request path)
%% stdio is the default transport; streamable HTTP is localhost-only.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as MCP client
    participant E as RIFT entrypoint
    participant S as RIFT server
    participant G as Retrieval engine
    participant D as Local index files

    C->>E: Start RIFT over stdio or connect over localhost HTTP
    E->>S: Start MCP transport
    S-->>C: Initialize and list tools
    C->>S: Call search, ask, or stats
    S->>G: Load lazy engine singleton
    G->>D: Read and validate FAISS and JSONL files
    D-->>G: Aligned local records
    G-->>S: JSON or extractive results
    S-->>C: Tool result with doc IDs and scores
    Note over C,D: No API keys, no LLM calls, no shell execution.
